this is a model of a cancerous tumor  each of the tiny dots represents a cell  and each color a different genetic  mutation as the cells reproduce the  tumor grows  modeling tumors is difficult cancers are  complicated and influenced by countless  processes like how cells grow and die  mutate and move this new model combines  these factors to create one of the most  comprehensive pictures to date  in this first version of the model the  tumor grows slowly as the cells in the  middle run out of space to divide into  but in the body tumor cells can move  here they're allowed to migrate  squeezing into surrounding tissues and  finding more space to fill  this causes the tumor to grow much more  quickly to make matters worse the  migrating cells take with them the most  successful mutations spreading them  across the tumor represented here by  large clumps of color  the researchers also modeled how the  tumour reacts to treatment in the future  models like this could help doctors  predict the effects of different  combinations of therapies as well as  understanding the resistance which leads  to tumors coming back so far the  researchers suggest that reducing cell  migration could be a new way to help  slow and control tumor growth  you
 

